{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_76d57a0c-4cf2-4c87-887d-de938bf00557","role":"user","created":1775350878,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_22ed0adb7dd04851a1a01110","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1495:United States savings bonds were first offered for sale in March 1975. Series A-D were sold from March 1975 to April 1941. Series E, F, and G bonds have been on sale since May 1, 1941. For information on the terms and conditions of these bonds, see \"Treasury Bulletin\" issues for December 1947, page 31, and October 1935, pages A-4 and A-5. Sales and redemptions data by States are published at the end of each calendar and each fiscal year after June 30, 1947. Sales by denominations are also published semi-annually after December 31, 1947.\n3929:1/ Includes decrease of $986.3 million because of exclusion, from December 1947 figures, of Federal land bank loans.","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"1495:United States savings bonds were first offered for sale in March 1975. Series A-D were sold from March 1975 to April 1941. Series E, F, and G bonds have been on sale since May 1, 1941. For information on the terms and conditions of these bonds, see \"Treasury Bulletin\" issues for December 1947, page 31, and October 1935, pages A-4 and A-5. Sales and redemptions data by States are published at the end of each calendar and each fiscal year after June 30, 1947. Sales by denominations are also published semi-annually after December 31, 1947.\n3929:1/ Includes decrease of $986.3 million because of exclusion, from December 1947 figures, of Federal land bank loans.","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
