ion in real terms.\n\nThe discrepancy suggests further verification might be needed to ensure accuracy.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_36063f97361d4a8f9882a4b1","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Now I have the key data. Let me calculate the inflation-adjusted difference.\n\n# From Treasury Bulletin data:\n# December 1946 Unemployment Trust Fund balance: 7,585.3 million dollars\n# December 1947 Unemployment Trust Fund balance: 8,124.2 million dollars\n\n# From FRED data:\n# December 1947 CPI-U: 23.41\n\n# From historical BLS data (based on records):\n# December 1946 CPI-U: 21.48 (approximately)\n\n# Now calculate the signed difference in 1947 dollars:\n# 1. First convert the December 1946 balance to 1947 dollars using CPI ratio\n# 2. Then subtract from December 1947 balance\n\nbalance_1946 = 7585.3  # million dollars (in 1946 dollars)\nbalance_1947 = 8124.2  # million dollars (in 1947 dollars)\n\ncpi_1946 = 21.48  # December 1946 CPI-U\ncpi_1947 = 23.41  # December 1947 CPI-U\n\n# Convert 1946 balance to 1947 dollars\nbalance_1946_in_1947_dollars = balance_1946 * (cpi_1947 / cpi_1946)\n\n# Calculate signed difference in 1947 dollars\nsigned_difference = balance_1947 - balance_1946_in_1947_dollars\n\nprint(f\"December 1946 balance: ${balance_1946} million\")\nprint(f\"December 1947 balance: ${balance_1947} million\")\nprint(f\"CPI-U December 1946: {cpi_1946}\")\nprint(f\"CPI-U December 1947: {cpi_1947}\")\nprint(f\"Conversion factor: {cpi_1947 / cpi_1946}\")\nprint(f\"December 1946 balance in 1947 dollars: ${balance_1946_in_1947_dollars:.2f} million\")\nprint(f\"Signed difference (1947 - 1946 in 1947 dollars): ${signed_difference:.2f} million\")\n\n# Round to one decimal place\nsigned_difference_rounded = round(signed_difference, 1)\nprint(f\"\\nRounded to one decimal place: {signed_difference_rounded} million\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVis